# ---- the spout ----
# Every face of the spout picks its own rectangle out of this one file, because a piece of geometry
# that pokes out past the block's own bounds has no sensible default UV. The map:
#
#     [0,0,4,3]    the mouth, bore and all      [8,0,10,2]   the nozzle's face, butter beading
#     [0,4,4,8]    the pipe's top               [8,2,10,5]   the nozzle's underside
#     [0,8,4,12]   the pipe's underside         [10,0,13,2]  the nozzle's cheeks
#     [4,4,8,7]    the pipe's cheeks
#
# Nothing shades the top lighter than the bottom here beyond a hint: Minecraft already multiplies a
# down face to 0.5 and the sides to 0.6-0.8, so painting the same falloff in would double it.
@texture block/infuser_spout 16x16 type=block
hjjhiiiijjjjjiii
juujiiiibbiiiiii
ijjiiiiiuuiiiiii
iiiiiiiiuuiiiiii
jhhjjjjjuuiiiiii
